    "title": "Today’s Wordle Hints for March 28, 2026",
    "text": "AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENTWordle Review No. 1,743Scroll down for hints and conversation about the puzzle for Saturday, March 28, 2026.VideoCreditCredit...Ben VoldmanBy New York Times GamesMarch 27, 2026Welcome to The Wordle Review. Be warned: This page contains spoilers for today’s puzzle. Solve Wordle first, or scroll at your own risk.Wordle is released at midnight in your time zone. In order to accommodate all time zones, there will be two Wordle Reviews published every day, dated based on Eastern Standard Time. If you find yourself reading the wrong review, check the number of your puzzle and go to this page to find the corresponding review.Need a Hint?Give me a consonantTGive me a vowelAOpen the comments section for more hints, scores and conversation from the Wordle community.Today’s DifficultyOur testers let us know how many guesses out of 6 it took them to solve the puzzle. If they miss the word, we count it as 7 guesses. They are paid to solve each puzzle in advance. Learn more about what they do.Today’s puzzle took our testers an average of 5.5 guesses out of 6, or very challenging.Your own experience may be different, tell us about it in the comments. For a deeper and more personalized analysis of your solve, please visit Wordle Bot.Today’s WordClick to revealOur Featured ArtistBen Voldman is a Paris-born illustrator and animator based in Brooklyn, N.Y. His work focuses on finding universal experiences that unite us in his belief that we have much more in common than what divides us. Lately, his work has centered on his love of New York City and the people and experiences that make it so beautiful. He is a graduate of the School of Visual Arts in New York, where he currently teaches.Further ReadingSee the archive for past and future posts.If you solved for a word different from what was featured today, please refresh your page.Join the conversation on social media. Use the hashtag #wordlereview to chat with other solvers.Leave any thoughts you have in the comments! Please follow community guidelines:Be kind. Comments are moderated for civility.If you run into any technical issues with the game, go to the Settings menu and tap “Report a bug.”See the Wordle Glossary for information on how to talk about Wordle.Want to talk about Spelling Bee? Check out our Spelling Bee Forum.Want to talk about Connections? Check out our Connections Companion.Trying to go back to the puzzle?AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENTThanks for reading The Times.Unlock your complimentary access.Activate now for unlimited articles courtesy of your school.No payment needed.",
